<%#
  The checkboxes behind "Change".

  Only opened by an admin who disagrees with what the columns implied, so it
  leads with the rule they are working to rather than an explanation of the
  feature: pick up to three, and each person has to be told apart by them.

  Three kinds of detail, and each box says which it is:
    - checked against the list (member number, ID number, name…);
    - a contact detail (email, phone): the secure voting service will not
      check those against anything, so choosing one sends a one-time code
      there instead, and that code is what proves the person;
    - an access code we hand out: fine for a simple vote, and the only thing
      a secret one cannot use at all.

  Every detail also says how many people on the list do not have it, because
  a list is usually missing a few emails and those people would silently lose
  their vote.

  Locals: `form` (any form including `ChoosesIdentifiers`), `name` (the
  parameter name to submit under), and optionally `options`, the details to
  render rows for. In the review state that is every detail a list can carry,
  because the columns are still being decided and the rows follow them live;
  rows for columns that are not kept are hidden.
%>
<% scope = "decidim.elections.vocdoni.admin.census_file.identifiers" %>
<% fields_mod = Decidim::Elections::Vocdoni::CensusCsv::Fields %>
<fieldset id="js-census-identifiers"
          class="vocdoni-census-file__fieldset vocdoni-identifiers"
          aria-describedby="census-identifiers-lead"
          data-weak="<%= fields_mod::WEAK.join(" ") %>">
  <legend class="sr-only"><%= t("legend", scope:) %></legend>
  <p class="help-text" id="census-identifiers-lead"><%= t("lead", scope:) %></p>

  <% available = form.identifier_options %>
  <% rows = local_assigns[:options] || available %>
  <p class="vocdoni-identifiers__empty" data-identifiers-empty <%= "hidden" if available.any? %>>
    <%= t("none_available", scope:) %>
  </p>

  <input type="hidden" name="<%= name %>[identifiers][]" value="">
  <ul class="vocdoni-identifiers__list">
    <% rows.each do |field| %>
      <%
        sends_code = form.sends_code?(field)
        secure_ok = form.usable_for_secure?(field)
        missing = form.people_without(field)
      %>
      <li class="vocdoni-identifiers__item"
          data-identifier="<%= field %>"
          data-identifier-sentence="<%= fields_mod.in_sentence(field) %>"
          <%= "hidden" unless available.include?(field) %>>
        <label class="vocdoni-identifiers__label" for="census_identifiers_<%= field %>">
          <input type="checkbox"
                 name="<%= name %>[identifiers][]"
                 id="census_identifiers_<%= field %>"
                 value="<%= field %>"
                 aria-describedby="census-identifiers-<%= field %>-hint"
                 <%= "checked" if form.identifier_selected?(field) %>>
          <span><%= fields_mod.label(field) %></span>
          <% if sends_code %>
            <span class="label success vocdoni-identifiers__badge"><%= t("sends_code", scope:) %></span>
          <% elsif !secure_ok %>
            <span class="label vocdoni-identifiers__badge"><%= t("simple_only", scope:) %></span>
          <% end %>
        </label>
        <p class="help-text vocdoni-identifiers__hint" id="census-identifiers-<%= field %>-hint">
          <span><%= t("options.#{field}", scope:, default: fields_mod.hint(field)) %></span>
          <%# The answer to "what happens to the members who don't have one?",
              with their own number, before they choose rather than after. %>
          <% if missing.positive? %>
            <span class="vocdoni-identifiers__missing"><%= t("missing", scope:, count: missing) %></span>
          <% end %>
        </p>
      </li>
    <% end %>
  </ul>

  <div class="vocdoni-identifiers__weak" data-identifiers-weak <%= "hidden" unless form.weak_identifiers? %>>
    <%= cell "decidim/announcement", t("weak", scope:), callout_class: "warning" %>
  </div>
</fieldset>
